Just a couple random thoughts that have been echoing through my nethack-
tortured transom...

In the SPOILERS (ah, the glorious spoiler file.. ah, those glorious charts)
the CARRYING CAPACITY of your character seems a bit... odd.  I mean, I'm 
assuming that most everyone has theirs set to HARD (and if you don't you're
a weenie and should be held upside down in a cage full of xans) and the 
spoilers state that a particular method (i.e. Method One...) is used.

Well, in my copy at least.. beyond a str of 18, str no longer matters in
the figuring of carrying capacity... what's more, according to the equation
laid out, you actually keep _more_ carrying capacity if you keep your str
at 18, because it drops dramatically at 18/01

Section from spoiler file follows:

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Strength | Carrying Capacity                                            |
|-------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| 1-18     | 5*level + 5*str - 10*(wounded legs)                          |
| 18/01-25 | 5*level(up to level 16) + 40 - 10*(wounded legs)             |
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Now, uh, check me on this.. but with an 18 str, by this formula at first
level, you should have a capacity of 95 (barring any wounded legs). 
However, with an 18/01! str, you only have a capacity of 45.  Is the
spoiler file wrong, or am I just seeing things after staring at a little @
symbol too long??

Oh, and.. one more question.. Just how _does_ that silly little infinite
capacity bag of holding trick work??


